      "body": "## Motivation\n\nPythonic streaming drops valid calls such as `[search(query=\"]\")]`. Non-streaming parsing handles them correctly.\n\n## Modifications\n\nIgnore brackets inside Python strings and comments when locating the call boundary. Add regressions for escapes, triple quotes, chunk boundaries and nested arguments.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n21 Pythonic CPU tests pass. All 5,310 chunk-partition checks match the expected arguments and non-streaming output.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Broader checks and environment</summary>\n\nThe full parser test file has 239 passing tests. The same 15 DeepSeek V3.2/V4 tests fail on both base and patch because tokenizer files are unavailable offline. No GPU serving or model-accuracy run.\n\nPython 3.12.3, OpenAI 2.6.1, xgrammar 0.2.7; existing CPU test environment uses Torch 2.13.0 rather than the project's 2.14.1.\n\n</details>\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot run. No performance claim.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with pre-commit (changed files).\n- [x] Add unit tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation (not needed; no public API change).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmarks (not run; parser-only CPU validation above).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38752107215](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38752107215)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38752107467](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38752107467)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38752107103](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38752107103)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
